+# Design frame
+
+The design frame renders real app components and the real theme through react-native-web, so a design review looks at the code that ships. It is dev-only and needs no daemon.
+
+## Run it
+
+```bash
+npm run design                     # http://localhost:8095/design
+DESIGN_PORT=8096 npm run design    # another port
+npm run design:check               # check every design file
+npm run design:check -- packages/app/src/design/designs/volume-meter.tsx
+```
+
+`npm run design` starts Expo web with `EXPO_PUBLIC_PASEO_DESIGN_FRAME=1`. It does not start or contact a daemon. Run `npm run build:app-deps` first in a fresh checkout.
+
+`/design` lists designs. `/design/<name>` opens one with the review bar:
+
+- **State**: the design's named states.
+- **Device**: Phone 375, Tablet 768, Desktop 1280, or All side by side.
+- **Zoom**: Fit scales the previews into the window; 100% shows them at device pixels.
+- **Theme**: every built-in theme, including Auto. Plugin themes need a host and are not offered.
+- **Check**: runs `design:check` on the design's file and shows the findings.
+
+The query string holds the selection, so a URL is a shareable review link: `/design/volume-meter?state=loud&device=all&theme=light`.
+
+## Add a design
+
+1. Copy `packages/app/src/design/templates/starter.tsx` to `packages/app/src/design/designs/<name>.tsx`.
+2. Register it in `packages/app/src/design/registry.ts` under the same `<name>`. Check finds the file by that name.
+3. Copy `templates/flow.md` next to it as `<name>.md` for the brief.
+4. Run `npm run design:check -- <file>` until it is clean.
+
+A design exports `{ title, states: [{ id, label, render }] }`. `render` is a component, so it can hold state and hooks. Compose with real components from `@/components`. `@/design/kit` has page, section, row and specimen layout pieces; they arrange examples and are not app UI. `useDesignFrame()` gives the preview's device and theme.
+
+Check rejects raw hex/rgb/hsl colors, `palette.*`, numeric padding/margin/gap/fontSize/lineHeight/fontWeight/borderRadius/borderWidth values (`0` is allowed), numeric icon `size={}` and `useUnistyles()`. Put `// design-check-ignore-next-line` above a line that has a reason to break a rule. The rules live in `packages/app/src/design/check/rules.ts`.
+
+`/design/catalog` is the design system reference: every color, spacing, type, icon, radius, border, shadow and opacity token read from the active theme, the `xs`/`sm`/`md` control sizes, and live shared components. Its Layout block shows the breakpoint and form factor each preview resolved to.
+
+## How it works
+
+- **No daemon.** The root layout (`packages/app/src/app/_layout.tsx`) renders `/design/*` through a bare provider tree with a `Slot`. Host runtime bootstrap, app chrome, the root stack, startup redirects and workspace restore never mount, so normal routing is untouched.
+- **Not in production.** Metro's `blockList` hides `src/app/design/` unless `EXPO_PUBLIC_PASEO_DESIGN_FRAME=1`, so Expo Router never sees the routes and nothing under `src/design` is bundled. The same flag gates the root layout branch at build time.
+- **Real breakpoints.** Each device preview is an iframe of the same route with `?frame=device`, sized to the device. Unistyles and `useIsCompactFormFactor()` read the iframe's window, so the phone is compact (`xs`) and tablet and desktop are wide (`md`, `xl`).
+- **Theme.** Each iframe is its own JS runtime. The review page posts the selected state and theme to every iframe, and each applies it through `applyTheme` from `packages/app/src/appearance/provider.tsx`, the path the app uses. Previews do not reload on change. Phone and tablet previews use the native default font sizes; desktop uses the web defaults.
+- **Check.** With the flag set, the Metro dev server answers `GET /__design/check?name=<design>` by running `packages/app/scripts/design-check.mjs`.
+
+## What web can't show
+
+Web is exact for the Electron and browser apps and close for iOS and Android.
+
+- `.native.tsx` variants never render. The web or base file renders in their place.
+- iOS and Android font metrics differ, so line heights and text widths shift by a few pixels.
+- Shadows render as CSS `box-shadow`; native shadow and Android elevation look different.
+- Haptics, keyboard avoidance, safe-area insets and native gestures are absent.
+- Hover works only in the browser. `Shortcut` and desktop tooltips are hidden on compact, as in the app.
+
+Confirm native-sensitive details on a device before calling a design done.
